 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spec-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse view: every specialty it knows, each with the veterinarians who hold it `[REQ-SPEC-001]`. All known specialties appear on one page, each under its stored name. Each veterinarian appears by full name — first name, then last name. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears under none of them; the page lists specialties, not the full veterinarian roster. The page is reached by its own address alone; this request adds no navigation entry and no link from another page. Like every page, its wording is presented in the reader's language (see [Language](#language)). This capability was stated by the product owner on 2026-08-08 rather than derived from observed behavior.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed by its stored name on a single page.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is shown as first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears under no specialty.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given unchanged stored data, when the directory is opened twice, then the specialties and the holders within each appear in the same order both times.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the directory, when it is opened, then it offers no search, no filter, and no page control.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by none.
+2. A clinic that knows no specialty renders the page with an empty list rather than failing.
+3. No page links to the specialty directory, so reaching it requires knowing its address.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
